{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"QUESTION 1 -- does rebar still use Success Criteria or Definition of Done?\n\nSuccess Criteria: YES, live. Epic/container clarity scoring (gates.py:136 + its lockstep copy det_floor.py:227), plan-review criteria G3/G5/G7/COH/F1, the author guide (writing-a-passing-plan.md:58,76), the completion verifier (completion_verifier.md:59), and code-review scope extraction (assemble.py:253).\n\nDefinition of Done: NO, not a real concept. Only prose in a P1 failure message (det_floor.py:191) and a free-text synonym the completion verifier honours if an author happens to write one. The blocking floor across all types is '## Acceptance Criteria' with >=1 '- [ ]' item."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1784950151094467001,"uuid":"1c649125-28d3-4d8a-af15-8de456f3c99d"}